   </title>
   <reference code="269651" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">SSC contributions in 2019 to framework conditions within food and agriculture in Kenya: &quot;5 &quot;.

Score from 1-5, 1 lowest and 5 highest.

The planned output targets in the project have been met in 2019.

The SSC programme has significantly contributed to the fulfilment of Outcome A, B and C in 2019. For outcome D there is still a way to go and activities to support this outcome will take off in 2020.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5"></target>
     <actual value="5"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased knowledge on the Danish control system at high level in Kenya</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="270940" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study tours to Denmark</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Workshops on risk based inceptions and audits"></target>
     <actual value="Four CCAs were supported in developing training guides for inspector based on the new philosophy of inspection- KeFs, MoH, PCPB, KDB."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="DFC courses"></target>
     <actual value="Kenya has been an active participant on the DFC courses for capacity building of national and county government technical personnel (food, and laboratory staff) involved in food safety control. Up to date, more than 400 personnel from partner organizations have been trained in Denmark in a wide-range of food safety topics including: Food safety in the dairy sector; Sustainable and Safe Livestock Production from Farm to Fork; Value Chains and Food Safety; Conflict Transformation; Global Health Challenges; One Health; Understanding Sustainability; Sustainable Food Systems; Microbial Food Quality and Safety and Food Safety Specialization."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Study tours to Denmark"></target>
     <actual value="One tour completed and one tour postponed due to COVID19"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Study tour for Head of Agencies"></target>
     <actual value="The Danish Veterinary and Food Administration facilitated a study tour. This helped shape the development of the proposed Food and Feed Safety Control Coordinating Bill and Policy."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
